-- title:
--   Supersingular deformation with monomial j when j(E₀)≠ 0,1728
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and an elliptic Weierstrass curve $E_0$ over $k$ (unit discriminant) such that $(0,0)$ is a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for the formal group $\widehat{E_0}$ taken $\bot$-adically: there is a unit $u\in k[[Z]]$ with $[q]_{\widehat{E_0}}=u\cdot \mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\,q\,0\,0$, where $[q]$ is the iterate `nthSeries` ($[0]=0$, $[n+1]=$ substitution of $([n],Z)$ into the group law); over a field this amounts to $[q]_{\widehat{E_0}}=\text{unit}\cdot Z^{q^2}$. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0:W_0\to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal, and assume $j(E_0)\neq 0$ and $j(E_0)\neq 1728$. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $\mathcal E$ over $W_0[[t]]$ with $\Delta_{\mathcal E}$ a unit whose reduction along $\mathrm{res}_0\circ(t\mapsto 0)$ is $E_0$; a commutative formal group $F^u$ over $W_0[[t]]$ whose law is $\mathcal E$'s Weierstrass law `formalGroupLawFixed` and which base changes along $\mathrm{res}_0\circ(t\mapsto0)$ to $\widehat{E_0}$; such that, writing $\gamma=\mathrm{coeff}_{Z^q}[q]_{F^u}\in W_0[[t]]$, one has $\mathrm{coeff}_{t}\,\gamma\equiv 1$ modulo the maximal ideal, $\gamma-u_1t\in q\,W_0[[t]]$ for some unit $u_1$, and $j(\mathcal E)-a_0=u_2t^{e}$ for some $a_0\in W_0$, $e\ge 1$ and unit $u_2$.
--
--   This is the case $j(E_0)\notin\{0,1728\}$ of the construction of a one-parameter Weierstrass deformation of a supersingular curve along which the $j$-invariant becomes a unit times a power of the parameter and the $q$-division datum is linear in the parameter modulo $q$. It feeds the unconditional statement [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_X_pow_of_five_le`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_X_pow_of_five_le), obtained by splitting on the value of $j(E_0)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_X_pow_of_five_le_of_j_ne_zero_of_j_ne.lean

